course: dictionary
lesson: 2297
title: Cringe: a word with many shades
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Cringe can do a few different jobs. It can mean to feel very embarrassed, to pull back from something scary or disgusting, or, in slang, to be awkward. Context tells you which one. «That video is so cringe» is slang: the clue is the video, and it means embarrassing.
explain: Look at this: «The mind often replays embarrassing moments at night; a "cringe attack" is slang for suddenly remembering something embarrassing.» The sentence explains the phrase for you, so you do not need a dictionary. Always ask: what does the sentence show about how someone feels?
explain: Cringe can also be a noun, a feeling you have. «A cringe of embarrassment» is one sharp moment of feeling embarrassed. Try swapping in embarrassed. If the sentence still makes sense, you have found the right meaning.
fact: Cringe is a verb, a noun and a slang adjective. Cringey and cringy are slang forms too.
fact: «Cringe» means to feel very embarrassed, often pulling a face or wanting to hide.
fact: «Cringe» can also mean to move back or bend away from something you are afraid of or find disgusting.
fact: Slang «cringe» means embarrassing or awkward, as in «That video is so cringe.»
fact: Useful phrases: «cringe with embarrassment», «cringe at», «cringe-worthy», and «the cultural cringe» (Australia), which means feeling your own culture is not as good as others.
exercise: «The little boy began to cringe when the whole class laughed at his dance.» What does cringe mean here? | Ate his lunch quickly | *Felt very embarrassed and wanted to hide | Shouted loudly | Did a happy twirl
exercise: Mia says the dad joke was so cringe. What does she mean? | It made everyone rich | It was very long | *It was embarrassing | It was a famous joke
exercise: In «a cringe of embarrassment», what kind of word is cringe? | A number | *A noun, a word for a feeling | A verb, a word for an action | An adjective, a word for a colour
test: The toddler began to cringe away from the buzzing wasp. What does cringe mean? | Clapped with joy | *Moved back from something scary or disgusting | Fell fast asleep | Sang a loud song
test: Ravi says his old school photo is cringe-worthy. What does he mean? | Worth lots of money | Very well lit and clear | *So embarrassing it makes you wince | Full of cheese
exam: «Turning a cringe into a shared joke takes the sting out.» Here cringe is most likely a noun meaning what? | A type of shoe | A happy song | *An embarrassing moment | A fast train
